        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1666c356-d06f-5849-bc27-6981e9375048",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Weinreich, Uriel Weinreich\n- Roles: linguists, sociolinguist, Yiddish scholar\n- Concepts: Yiddish, sociolinguistics, “A language is a dialect with an army and navy”\n- Products: Modern Yiddish-English English-Yiddish Dictionary\n\nFacts:\n- Max Weinreich was born on 22 April 1894 in Kuldīga in the Russian Empire, now Latvia.\n- Uriel Weinreich was born on 23 May 1926 and was a Polish-American linguist.\n- Max Weinreich was a Russian Jewish linguist who specialized in sociolinguistics and Yiddish.\n- Max Weinreich was the father of the linguist Uriel Weinreich.\n- Uriel Weinreich edited the Modern Yiddish-English English-Yiddish Dictionary.\n- Max Weinreich popularized the adage “A language is a dialect with an army and navy” after hearing it from an audience member at one of his lectures.\n- Uriel Weinreich died on 30 March 1967.\n- Max Weinreich died on 29 January 1969 in New York City, United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
